            <ArticleTitle>Successful resuscitation of patient with massive coronary air embolism occluding two vessels during coronary angiography--a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>155-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Massive coronary air embolism is usually disastrous although successful resuscitation has been reported previously. To what extent a patient with coronary air embolism can be resuscitated is not known. The authors report a rare case of massive air embolism to the left coronary arteries and successful resuscitation by vigilantly maintaining an effective driving force to dissipate the air lock.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
